# ClipForge

Existing SaaS at this repo. Read `docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`, `docs/FEATURE_STATUS.md`, and `docs/ROADMAP.md` before adding features. Commit `bcb4bb3` is the audited baseline. Do not scaffold a new app or swap the architecture.

## Stack

- Next.js App Router, TypeScript, PostgreSQL, Prisma. Auth is custom scrypt sessions in `src/server/auth/`, not Auth.js or Supabase, until a replacement is approved.
- Tailwind and shadcn are not installed. Styles live in `app/globals.css`.
- Storage today is memory or gitignored `.local-media/`. No S3 client.
- FFmpeg rendering lives in `src/lib/render/`. Keep FFmpeg out of request handlers.
- Redis, BullMQ, and a real email provider are not wired up. Add them only when a feature needs them.
- Razorpay is the only payment gateway. Prices and recipient caps are in `src/lib/billing/catalog.ts`. Do not change them without approval.

## Safety

- Official APIs only. Never collect or store Instagram passwords.
- Do not create AWS resources, deploy, or upgrade a cloud plan without explicit approval. See `docs/COST_GUARDRAILS.md`.
- Do not commit `.env`, keys, tokens, or `.local-media/`. `.env.example` stays placeholders.
- Do not rewrite git history, force-push, or push unless the owner asks in that message.
- Prisma 7.10 rejects Node 23. Use Node 22.12+ (22.23.4 worked). `npm test` is not a Next.js or PostgreSQL test.

## How to change code

Business rules stay pure in `src/lib/domain/`. Handlers go through session, validation, ownership, plan limits, then a version-checked save. Someone else's object is a 404.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — trust the client for the user id
const userId = body.userId;

// ✅ GOOD — session only
const userId = requireUser(ctx);
```

Published cycle items are immutable. Edits apply to upcoming items only. Re-check share permissions before render, import, and publish.

Work in small steps: read the existing code, change the smallest surface, update tests, run the relevant command, and report the real exit status.
